# Check files out exactly as committed, on every machine.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners, like Git for Windows by default, set
# core.autocrlf=true, which turns every LF into CRLF on checkout. makepkg
# refuses to source a PKGBUILD containing CRLF, and patches have to apply byte
# for byte. "-text" switches that conversion off whatever the local git
# configuration says. Unlike "text eol=lf" it never rewrites a file on commit
# either, so a patch against sources with CRLF lines keeps them.
* -text
